  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be a point on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The normal to the parabola at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> meets the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>. The area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> is the focus of the parabola, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math>. If the slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> of the normal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> are both positive integers, then the pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
