  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>,</p><p>Now plotting the normal to parabola at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a716b152-dac5-4209-b751-0649f2b39468.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 219px;\" /></p><p>So, equation of normal at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Hence, point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And focus of parabola will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now finding the area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math></p><p>So, possible pair from option will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;which&nbsp;satisfies above equation</p></blockquote>",
